Based on the DHD code flow we discussed, I would not change the business flow. The safest codebase change is around the PDF merge layer + exception handling + logging.

Exact codebase changes

1. PDFUtility.java — pdfMergeToFile()

Current critical operation is essentially:

mergedDoc.getPages().add(addedPdf.getPages());

Change this to process each input PDF independently:

for (String pdfFile : pdfFiles) {
    try {
        Document addedPdf = new Document(pdfFile);
        mergedDoc.getPages().add(addedPdf.getPages());
        addedPdf.close();
        logger.info("Successfully merged PDF: {}", pdfFile);
    } catch (Exception e) {
        logger.error(
            "Failed to merge PDF: {}. Continuing with remaining PDFs.",
            pdfFile,
            e
        );
        // continue with next PDF
    }
}

Purpose: If one PDF has the problematic annotation structure, the complete ZIP should not immediately fail during merge.

