6. AWSDocumentServiceHelper.java — convertEPICZipToPDFS3()

The current outer catch is effectively catching the merge failure and moving the ZIP to unprocessed.

The improvement should be to distinguish:

ZIP extraction
      ↓
PDF transformation
      ↓
PDF merge
      ↓
Output validation
      ↓
S3 upload

rather than treating everything as one generic exception.

For example:

try {
    // transform PDFs
    try {
        pdfUtility.pdfMergeToFileWithBlankPage(...);
    } catch (PdfMergeException e) {
        logger.error(
            "PDF merge failed for EPIC case: {}",
            caseId,
            e
        );
        // apply existing partial-processing/business handling
    }
    // validate final PDF
    // upload to S3
} catch (Exception e) {
    logger.error(
        "Exception occurred while processing EPIC ZIP for case: {}",
        caseId,
        e
    );
    // existing failure handling
}

The exact implementation depends on your existing partial-processing framework.

