So the Jira code changes I would put

Codebase changes:

1. PDFUtility.pdfMergeToFile()
    * Add per-PDF exception handling.
    * Log the exact source PDF that fails.
    * Continue processing only according to existing partial-processing rules.
2. PDFUtility.pdfMergeToFileWithBlankPage()
    * Preserve existing blank-page positioning.
    * Improve merge-stage logging.
3. Merged PDF validation
    * Validate output exists, is non-empty, and can be reopened before marking processing successful.
4. AWSDocumentServiceHelper.convertEPICZipToPDFS3()
    * Separate merge exceptions from the generic ZIP processing exception.
    * Ensure the failure is logged with case ID + PDF filename + full stack trace.
5. Aspose
    * Check current Aspose PDF version and approved upgrade/fix for invalid annotation dictionaries.
    * Test annotation/form normalization or flattening only if required and approved.

Most important point

I would make #1 + #3 + #4 first. These are definite code-quality/robustness improvements based on the logs.

The annotation flattening/removal is not yet an exact fix, because the radio button is only a suspected trigger. We need to reproduce it with an approved non-production PDF before changing the document contents.
